WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:01.149
Finally we’ve made it.

00:00:01.149 --> 00:00:04.130
For over at least the past 9 months we've
been on this amazing journey, like I think

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:08.610
I started Jujutsu Kaisen when I was around
the 30k mark which is truly insane to me that

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:12.920
we’re here now, so thank you for all the
growth with this series and others i've covered!

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:17.689
BUT YES for the first time here we are catching
upto the current happenings inside of the

00:00:17.689 --> 00:00:20.119
unforgivable world that is Jujutsu Kaisen...

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:25.760
Its really funny to me cause every part in
this story seems to ‘in my eyes at least’

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:29.230
dwarf what happened previously and this section
of the story is no exception.

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:34.250
Infact in my eyes it sets up everything for
what I believe to be the final year of Jujutsu

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:35.250
Kaisen.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:38.450
Especially if we stick with what Gege has
given us time frame wise.

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:41.921
BUT enough of me yarning about this amazing
series, if you are new around here then make

00:00:41.921 --> 00:00:46.260
sure to subscribe and also push this video
to 5k likes and ill drop the full Jujutsu

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:51.320
Kaisen story (so far) kicking off where the
anime ended, next weekend.

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:55.610
Either way I hope you enjoy the video, now
lets get into it!

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:57.600
So!

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:01.870
remember how we left things with Yuji and
his group.

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:06.340
Well as the influx of American soldiers entered
the culling game a multitude of kogane’s

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:09.170
appeared and begin registering the soldiers
as new players.

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:13.960
Elsewhere, Kenjaku and Uraume are seen at
the Zenin clan’s warehouse, where surprisingly

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:18.100
its explained that there is a secret way to
transfer between colonies.

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:21.390
Simply they cannot leave unless they answered
the kogane’s call.

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:26.360
Unimpressed, Uraume instead suggested that
the space would be more suitable as the ‘bath’

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:27.600
for Sukuna’s revival.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:32.259
Flying back over to the troops as they invade
Remi’s room, which is just the biggest L

00:01:32.259 --> 00:01:36.759
for her ngl, in military fashion they throw
a flashbang before rushing in and trying to

00:01:36.759 --> 00:01:41.110
immobilize her with a tazer allowing them
to easily inject her with a sedative.

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:45.870
Outside, groups of soldiers are seen remarking
that the sorcerers were nothing special and

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:49.420
simply wondered why their lieutenant was so
worried about the operation.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:52.829
Rolling up, we see another group of soldiers
who’d taken out their target instead of

00:01:52.829 --> 00:01:54.530
capturing them as ordered.

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:58.299
The soldier in-charge rebuked her, but the
latter flippantly said that it didn’t matter

00:01:58.299 --> 00:01:59.720
since the brain was unharmed.

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:04.120
She further complained that literally nothing
worked against the sorcerer, and even a 50

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:06.740
calibre bullet didn’t pierce the target’s
skin.

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:10.920
So remember the helicopter dude Yuji absolutely
pummelled, well that's actually the person

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:12.590
her squad took out here.

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:16.780
Having heard the dude had a helicopter head,
the soldier was hesitant to believe her until

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:19.540
he saw just how damaged the females comrades
were.

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:24.230
In the end she concluded that there must be
sorcerers of various power levels and she

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:25.890
got stuck with some of the tougher ones.

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:28.500
WHICH AS WE KNOW IS JUST HILARIOUS.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:37.340
THINKING HABA IS OP IS ACTUALLY TO GOOD, CANT
WAIT TILL THEY FIND A GRADED SORCERER.

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:42.200
Funnily enough we pop over and see the ruffian
Hazenoki exploding some poor unsuspecting

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:44.989
soldiers vehicle as they rolled by.

00:02:44.989 --> 00:02:49.560
Noticing that the enemy was a foreigner, the
sorcerer remembered Reggie’s words and wondered

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:52.870
if this was the “bomb” he suspected Kenjaku
would drop.

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:56.840
Now back with the megalomaniac himself and
Uraume, the latter guessed that the cursed

00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:00.540
energy of every colony could be increased
by pitting sorcerers against non-sorcerers,

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:03.360
ending the custom before the merger with Tengen.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:08.569
Kenjaku admitted that what Uraume guessed
was only 60 percent of his plan, elaborating

00:03:08.569 --> 00:03:12.720
that the cursed energy levels in every colony
except Tokyo and Sendai were still insufficient.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:13.720
SO WHO ELSE ARE WE GONNA MEET, That's literally
Gege being like ‘well guys n gals there's

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:14.720
another 5 or so colonies that need to be kicked
up a notch.’

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:18.830
Also Kenjaku did only say that Tokyo was the
battle ground to the US, so im assuming they

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:24.050
aren't anywhere else other than there in Tokyo
colony 1 or 2 BUT we will find out later.

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:28.260
What's actually even funnier about the military
is that Kenjaku had only sent in the foreign

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:33.170
military as insurance and was already that
the fighting would not be very intense.

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:37.670
Having manifested a curse to clean up the
mess that was Ogi Zenin, Kenjaku claimed that,

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:41.650
unlike the reincarnated players, those who
had only recently awakened their cursed techniques

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:46.180
would be reluctant to fight and may even retreat
if they get to many casualties.

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:49.920
Uraume questioned if the military had been
sent in at night to give them an advantage

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:54.849
and also since non-Japanese individuals would
not release cursed energy.

00:03:54.849 --> 00:03:59.829
Yet its actually revealed, that in the moment
of passing there’s an exception as the stress

00:03:59.829 --> 00:04:02.720
of seeing curses pushes them to a new level.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:08.730
Its also considered natural law that non-sorcerers
cant win against jujutsu sorcery.

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:14.019
As one poor poor American soldier notices
a terrifying cursed spirit, it further goes

00:04:14.019 --> 00:04:18.060
in-depth that Kenjaku had released multiple
cursed spirits in every colony that are specifically

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:22.639
active only at night to force out that higher
level of cursed energy from these new soldiers.

00:04:22.639 --> 00:04:27.480
Back over with our main crew, Angel quickly
deduced that Kenjaku had sent in non-sorcerers

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:31.570
to be killed by cursed spirits as a failsafe
to produce more cursed energy.

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:35.539
Having left the room and made their way down
some stairs, the group run into an empty cafeteria

00:04:35.539 --> 00:04:40.070
right as a stun grenade lands in front of
them.

00:04:40.070 --> 00:04:44.150
Noticing it, Yuji quickly kicks the flashbang
away before it could explode..

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:48.150
Seeing a squad pull up, Megumi initially assumed
that the soldiers were trying to protect people,

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:51.570
but instantly discarded the possibility as
the soldiers without a second thought began

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:54.060
shooting at the sorcerers.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:58.850
Abruptly we see what seems to be a passed
memory from of a cursed spirit feeding three

00:04:58.850 --> 00:05:01.229
young children inside an abandoned building.

00:05:01.229 --> 00:05:07.180
Then back with the group we see good old Megumi
interrogating a Japanese soldier, who was

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:09.949
acting as a guide for the foreign military
forces.

00:05:09.949 --> 00:05:14.220
When Hana asks why Japan had not taken the
opportunity to become energy self-sufficient

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:18.880
sooner, the soldier responds that the Jujutsu
HQ controlling the country is too proud and

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:24.440
everyone here is obsessed with self-responsibility,
so it would have never caught on with other

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:25.440
countries.

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:29.140
Megumi realized that Kenjaku had only lured
the military to the colonies under the false

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:33.669
pretence that cursed energy was up for grabs
as another energy source.

00:05:33.669 --> 00:05:37.539
Megumi deducts that the soldiers’ deaths
would increase cursed energy in the colonies

00:05:37.539 --> 00:05:42.229
and complete the ritual preceding Tengen’s
merger with the wider Japanese population.

00:05:42.229 --> 00:05:47.039
Megumi is so damn big brain that the dude
even suspects that Kenjaku has likely orchestrated

00:05:47.039 --> 00:05:50.010
the Culling Game as a distraction for his
true plan.

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:54.130
Stepping in Yuji asks if they should help
them, prompting Takaba to ask why they should

00:05:54.130 --> 00:05:57.570
help the people who wanted to abduct them
for experiments.

00:05:57.570 --> 00:06:01.539
Megumi reasons that if they allow Kenjaku
to fulfil the ritual, everyone would be caught

00:06:01.539 --> 00:06:02.900
up in the merger with Tengen.

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:07.229
Yet, Angel cuts in telling them its no use
since Tokyo No.1 colony has already reached

00:06:07.229 --> 00:06:09.479
the required level of cursed energy.

00:06:09.479 --> 00:06:13.690
Yuji challenges the Angel’s decision, stating
that it did not invalidate their saving lives.

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:20.100
The latter explains that it has a symbiotic
relationship with its vessel, so putting Hana

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:25.530
at unnecessary risk is akin to putting the
curse living within her body at risk.

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:29.470
Shooting over we see the true terror some
soldiers are being put through.

00:06:29.470 --> 00:06:33.730
After having fun with its first soldier, the
predatory curse picked up its next prey, which

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:37.360
just happens to be the Japanese soldier the
group was interrogating before.

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:42.160
Laying there and suspecting the worst, the
soldier thinks back to the times he had believed

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:46.669
that he was ready to pass on, but feels that
now, this is different and seeing what awaits

00:06:46.669 --> 00:06:49.410
him truly shatters his resolve.

00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:53.050
Nearby Yuji and Megumi just happen to be running
through an alley.

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:57.001
Megumi insists to his boy doesn't need to
be so hostile, and asks if Yuji’s comment

00:06:57.001 --> 00:07:01.330
about not trusting Hana was a reference to
beings like Sukuna and Angel.

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:07.569
So referring back to that random flashback,
well it was actually Hana as a child.

00:07:07.569 --> 00:07:11.220
Sadly she had been forced to live with the
cursed spirit for almost a year.

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:15.810
Eventually though she managed to escape after
following a white dog with a fluffy tail.

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:20.380
Of course it was no one other than Megumi’s
white divine dog who led her to safety before

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:22.510
returning to him and Gojo.

00:07:22.510 --> 00:07:27.050
As Hana watches the 3 reunite and begin to
leave it flashes back to the present as she

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:29.120
remembers their kindness.

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:34.590
In turn she’s decided to try and help people
herself as she always believed that someday

00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:37.870
they would meet again and she would proudly
stand by his side.

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:41.919
Back in the alley now, all Megumi wanted was
for Yuji to be a bit more considerate.

00:07:41.919 --> 00:07:47.800
To which after hearing this, our boy confesses
that ever since they regrouped, he was scared

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:52.230
that Hana would take Nobara’s place.

00:07:52.230 --> 00:07:57.360
WHICH OML WE ACTUALLY GOT SOME MORE NOBARA
CRUMBS, GEGE KNOWS WE ARE DAMN FEIGNS WANTING

00:07:57.360 --> 00:08:00.889
ABSOLUTELY ANYTHING TO DO WITH HER OR GOJO.

00:08:00.889 --> 00:08:05.099
As Megumi scolds Yuji and asks him to apologize
to Hana, the queen herself appears before

00:08:05.099 --> 00:08:08.440
the boys, bringing the group fully back together.

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:12.669
LET THE RIPENING BEGING...

00:08:12.669 --> 00:08:16.620
As huge beams of light emerge from every colony
throughout Japan, it begins attracting the

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:19.500
attention of everyone throughout the country.

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:23.449
Not understanding what's happening, many people
just note that something doesn't feel right,

00:08:23.449 --> 00:08:25.960
like the air had become unnaturally dry.

00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:29.830
returning to our crew, Maki gives everyone
a full rundown of everything that's happened

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:31.280
up until this point.

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:35.000
She explained that Choso had managed to protect
the back-gate of the Prison Realm, but relayed

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:37.860
the news of Yuki’s defeat and Tengen’s
capture.

00:08:37.860 --> 00:08:43.729
In another location our boy Choso clutching
the back gate or literally hope itself, weeps

00:08:43.729 --> 00:08:46.410
as Kirara asked him about Yuki’s whereabouts.

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:49.250
Pretty much to me at least confirming her
demise.

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:52.770
Maki further told the two first-years that
the ritual preceding the merger had ended,

00:08:52.770 --> 00:08:54.020
leaving the boys shocked with just how much
has happened.

00:08:54.020 --> 00:08:57.459
Calmly, Maki concluded that taking down the
villain would be a challenge, leading Yuji

00:08:57.459 --> 00:09:00.209
to wonder why the merger hadn’t started
yet.

00:09:00.209 --> 00:09:05.589
Angel points out to the group that sorcerers
could probably reject the merger with their

00:09:05.589 --> 00:09:08.325
cursed energy, so because of that nothing
is going on around them; however it may be

00:09:08.325 --> 00:09:09.325
a completely different case outside of the
colonies.

00:09:09.325 --> 00:09:13.170
Being able to travel inside and out of the
barriers though Maki disagrees and informs

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:17.560
them that apart from a few affected people,
most of Japan population is unaffected as

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:18.930
of now.

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:23.300
Megumi suspected that Kenjaku either couldn’t
start the merger yet, or didn't want to; however,

00:09:23.300 --> 00:09:29.320
since there was no way to find out, they decided
to focus on freeing Tsumiki first.

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:34.690
The big man himself, intervened listing off
the four rules they they had decided to implement.

00:09:34.690 --> 00:09:38.300
Megumi again clarifies that rule one does
indeed subject a player to curse technique

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:42.760
removal or subsequently death thru something
messing with the brain, the purpose of this

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:47.240
first rule was just to start fights with people.

00:09:47.240 --> 00:09:51.110
Maki remarked thought that it was actually
rules 2 and 3 which were tricky as they involved

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:54.670
somehow creating a form of movement and communication
across colonies.

00:09:54.670 --> 00:09:59.050
Stepping forth herself, Hana declares that
she could move across the colonies by virtue

00:09:59.050 --> 00:10:00.649
of the Angel’s cursed technique.

00:10:00.649 --> 00:10:05.070
Maki asked if she could use the technique
on someone else to help them leave, but the

00:10:05.070 --> 00:10:09.090
voice of Angel replied that they could only
extinguish a barrier technique by destroying

00:10:09.090 --> 00:10:10.470
the root of the barrier itself.

00:10:10.470 --> 00:10:15.579
If they cant locate the so called root, they’re
only able to pass through the colonies without

00:10:15.579 --> 00:10:16.579
destroying it.

00:10:16.579 --> 00:10:20.910
With the group realizing that adding new rules
might not allow them to move across colonies,

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:24.850
they decided to add the fourth rule and focus
on allowing players to withdraw from the game

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:25.850
entirely.

00:10:25.850 --> 00:10:30.340
So earlier on and id say it was before they
left the Hotel, Yuta had transferred all the

00:10:30.340 --> 00:10:34.530
accumulated points over to Megumi, bringing
his total number of points up to 359.

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:40.520
Btw this is actually a mess up by Gege here
but notice that it already says 1 rule?

00:10:40.520 --> 00:10:46.399
well Gege messed up and spoiled everyone in
some way letting them know that INDEED Megumi

00:10:46.399 --> 00:10:47.639
would create a rule!

00:10:47.639 --> 00:10:51.610
Speaking up Megumi attempts to add a rule
allowing players to withdraw from the game,

00:10:51.610 --> 00:10:55.649
but the Kogane rejected it, stating that it
clashed against rule 7.

00:10:55.649 --> 00:10:59.529
Megumi tried again, asking if the rule would
allow players to withdraw if they invited

00:10:59.529 --> 00:11:02.329
a substitute into the colony to take their
place.

00:11:02.329 --> 00:11:08.130
BUT STILL Kogane refused, however out of nowhere
its states that the culling game has a suggestion.

00:11:08.130 --> 00:11:12.089
It says it would indeed let players leave
the game on the condition they provided one

00:11:12.089 --> 00:11:15.300
substitute and spent 100 points.

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:20.010
Unable to negotiate further and utterly peeved
with the result, Megumi agreed, despite knowing

00:11:20.010 --> 00:11:24.450
that the new rule would require them to take
out at least another 20 sorcerers to just

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:25.450
leave.

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:29.100
With all of negotiations complete, Megumi
created a new rule.

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:33.810
Rule 11 - A player can leave the game by expending
100 points to invite a new player into the

00:11:33.810 --> 00:11:35.920
colony as a substitute.

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:43.839
Looking over to the clan killer, Megumi asks
if its okay for her to transport Tsumiki to

00:11:43.839 --> 00:11:45.740
the Tokyo No. 1 colony.

00:11:45.740 --> 00:11:49.470
Yuji asked if it would be safer to transfer
the points to her remotely, since she was

00:11:49.470 --> 00:11:51.260
already outside the colonies.

00:11:51.260 --> 00:11:55.519
However, Megumi pointed out that since the
rules illicitly stated that a must declare

00:11:55.519 --> 00:11:59.730
their participation in a colony within 19
days, trying to circumvent it might lead to

00:11:59.730 --> 00:12:03.180
his sister being subject to curse technique
removal when she tries to leave the game.

00:12:03.180 --> 00:12:08.750
Flashing forth to the fateful day of November
16 we see that after reconnecting with Tsumiki,

00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:14.500
Maki led her and the assistant manager Ijichi
to to outskirts of Tokyo colony No.1.

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:21.019
So when it comes to who’s gonna be the substitute,
Ijichi had previously agreed to take the role

00:12:21.019 --> 00:12:24.899
as due to Maki’s lack of cursed energy it
prevents the barriers from recognizing her

00:12:24.899 --> 00:12:27.540
or allowing her to become a substitute.

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:31.459
Tsumiki is visibly conflicted by the idea,
but Ijichi reasoned that they didn't have

00:12:31.459 --> 00:12:36.570
enough time to find someone else as its literally
been 16 days since everything begun only giving

00:12:36.570 --> 00:12:39.420
her 3 days before she fully assimilates.

00:12:39.420 --> 00:12:43.600
Standing there, Ijichi reminisces on past
memories and how he always wanted to be a

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:45.279
sorcerer that helped people.

00:12:45.279 --> 00:12:49.320
Yet Gojo demanded he get his license and become
a manager.

00:12:49.320 --> 00:12:53.760
Ijichi had thought the sorcerer to be harsh
back then, but now realized that he would

00:12:53.760 --> 00:13:00.690
have been dead by now if he continues down
the path he’d previously chosen.

00:13:00.690 --> 00:13:07.209
So remember the spawn glitch Yuji and Megumi
went thru along with everyone else, WELL SOMEHOW

00:13:07.209 --> 00:13:11.680
Tsumiki hacked the game and got insanely lucky
abruptly appearing before Megumi and Yuji

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:14.280
upon entering the barrier, completely stunning
them.

00:13:14.280 --> 00:13:20.720
With no time to lose in his eyes, Megumi transferred
a hundred points to his sister, asking her

00:13:20.720 --> 00:13:22.980
to declare her withdrawal from the game...

00:13:22.980 --> 00:13:28.450
However, to their shock, Tsumiki used the
points to instead add a new rule.

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:32.500
She immediately makes the 12th rule granting
players unrestricted entry and exit across

00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:33.850
colony borders.

00:13:33.850 --> 00:13:38.660
Mortified and literally just standing there
unable to fathom what happen Megumi asks his

00:13:38.660 --> 00:13:44.470
grinning sister who in the world she really
was.

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:45.470
SO YESSS, DID I MENTION THIS WAS KENJAKU’s
WORLD?

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:46.470
Everyone just hold onto you’re damn seats,
there is a reason this set of chapters relates

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:47.470
directly back to episode 7…

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:48.470
Have you ever felt true pain???

00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:51.680
In those few moments before what we now know
as true pain crawled its way out of the dark

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:52.680
abyss.

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:57.459
Yuji just assumed everything was sweet, now
Tsumiki was safe, Megumi would be all right,

00:13:57.459 --> 00:14:01.529
Angel would follow up after and then kill
Sukuna along with Yuji and release Gojo, who

00:14:01.529 --> 00:14:03.450
would in turn take care of Kenjaku.

00:14:03.450 --> 00:14:09.190
The plan had no faults, apart from the fact
that they don't own the paying field.

