from the Harima province…

00:27:43.250 --> 00:27:47.490
WHICH is what I was referring to before and
goes back to Kenjaku using a binding vow on

00:27:47.490 --> 00:27:57.090
using Yuji at birth or even before.

00:27:57.090 --> 00:28:02.610
We know he purposefully found a bloodline
that has some form of durability, possibly

00:28:02.610 --> 00:28:08.789
to keep Sukuna safe during his time in Yuji,
and now its confirmed that Yuji’s true heritage

00:28:08.789 --> 00:28:11.649
originates from a family in the Harima province.

00:28:11.649 --> 00:28:15.909
This Harima province was established in the
600s AD and ran upto the late 1800’s before

00:28:15.909 --> 00:28:16.909
it merged into a bunch of different districts.

00:28:16.909 --> 00:28:18.370
So im assuming he’s from a time before the
golden age of sorcery and could've even been

00:28:18.370 --> 00:28:20.410
an old family in the Jujutsu would that used
to be a top contender but supposedly died

00:28:20.410 --> 00:28:21.410
out over the ages.

00:28:21.410 --> 00:28:22.460
Ya thought the arc ended here??

00:28:22.460 --> 00:28:27.400
no no no, Sukuna as Megumi speed run this
damn bath and after having arrived at the

00:28:27.400 --> 00:28:32.590
Zenin’s household we see him falling deeper
and deeper into evil itself.

00:28:32.590 --> 00:28:37.490
Outside the bath Uraume dressed up ritual
robes asks Kenjaku whether or not he plans

00:28:37.490 --> 00:28:38.659
to end the culling game.

00:28:38.659 --> 00:28:43.130
To which its explains that his assimilation
of the wider population cant actually happen

00:28:43.130 --> 00:28:44.570
until the game ends.

00:28:44.570 --> 00:28:48.470
The reason the culling game was even able
to be constructed in the first place was because

00:28:48.470 --> 00:28:52.299
Kenjaku had shouldered the burden of an equally
unreasonable binding vow.

00:28:52.299 --> 00:28:56.659
Yet instead of getting on with ending it,
currently, he’s more interested in Sukuna’s

00:28:56.659 --> 00:28:58.210
“bath” and its workings.

00:28:58.210 --> 00:29:02.260
Kenjaku himself knew that The ‘bath’ was
originally a ritual to transform vessels that

00:29:02.260 --> 00:29:05.299
had been treasured as family heirlooms into
cursed tools.

00:29:05.299 --> 00:29:09.559
To do this the clan must make a solution of
cursed energy which is created by straining

00:29:09.559 --> 00:29:12.500
organisms chosen in a Kodoku ritual.

00:29:12.500 --> 00:29:16.600
Once that is prepared the vessels are soaked
for 10 months and 10 days in the solution.

00:29:16.600 --> 00:29:20.919
So what's really cool about this Ritual is
that its actually something from real Japanese

00:29:20.919 --> 00:29:21.919
folklore.

00:29:21.919 --> 00:29:25.990
Its a derivative of the Chinese Gu magic and
is a type of poisons ability.

00:29:25.990 --> 00:29:31.460
In reality To create Kodoku, sorcerers would
mix several insects in a jar, and let them

00:29:31.460 --> 00:29:33.990
kill one another until only one survived.

00:29:33.990 --> 00:29:37.941
The fluids of the insect that survived would
be used to poison an individual with a curse

00:29:37.941 --> 00:29:40.710
that would control them, cause them misfortune,
or kill them.

00:29:40.710 --> 00:29:44.750
The remaining insect could also be used as
a sort of "luck charm" granting the one who

00:29:44.750 --> 00:29:47.029
performed the ritual great wealth.

00:29:47.029 --> 00:29:50.690
This ritual could also be used as a death
curse by giving the riches to an ignorant

00:29:50.690 --> 00:29:51.690
individual.

00:29:51.690 --> 00:29:58.920
(perhaps Kenjaku is the ignorant one here)
The term "Kodoku" can also be applied to the

00:29:58.920 --> 00:30:02.320
spirit which is the incarnation of this particular
magic.

00:30:02.320 --> 00:30:08.350
Funnily enough, the technique was used in
the Nara Period, which is as we know the era

00:30:08.350 --> 00:30:12.180
just before the golden age of Jujutsu Sorcery.

00:30:12.180 --> 00:30:17.610
Kenjaku was actually surprised that they specifically
chose curses, especially for the fact that

00:30:17.610 --> 00:30:19.559
the become dust apon their deaths.

00:30:19.559 --> 00:30:24.049
Uraume though, like the cold queen she is
figured out a way around this.

00:30:24.049 --> 00:30:27.789
Simply if she carefully pins down the spirits
before freezing theirs cores, they don't turn

00:30:27.789 --> 00:30:31.690
to dust and it allows them to strain away
the toxins they need.

00:30:31.690 --> 00:30:35.809
Confused with the purpose of it all, Kenjaku
asks why and Uraume just tells him its to

00:30:35.809 --> 00:30:37.520
get closer to evil.

00:30:37.520 --> 00:30:41.850
The entire purpose of this ritual is to suppress
Megumi Fushiguro’s soul deeper into the

00:30:41.850 --> 00:30:42.850
depths.

00:30:42.850 --> 00:30:46.960
As the further down he sinks the easier it
is for Sukuna to control the cage he’s currently

00:30:46.960 --> 00:30:47.960
controlling.

00:30:47.960 --> 00:30:51.940
Having completed the bath, the Demon Lord
himself rises from the depths of evil, symbolizing

00:30:51.940 --> 00:30:55.630
that Megumi Fushiguro has lost the small hold
he had over Sukuna!

00:30:55.630 --> 00:30:59.370
Kenjaku questions why he didnt change his
appearance, but Sukuna just reasons that if

00:30:59.370 --> 00:31:03.169
he’s gonna be battling sorcerers then its
better to maintain Megumi’s appearance.

00:31:03.169 --> 00:31:06.799
Honestly this is probably for the fact that
whenever he runs into a group of people from

00:31:06.799 --> 00:31:12.340
